# API Routes — VTC Apps

For **platform ZAPI** calls from static Vite apps, use the catalog instead of app-owned routes: `zapi-developer-catalog.mdc` (`GET /api/v1/developer/catalog`). This file applies to **Next.js `src/app/api/`** routes only.

Auth: `?token=` on every request — `auth-bootstrap.mdc`. List params: `business-patterns.mdc`. Scoping: `app-types.mdc`.

## Layout

```
src/app/api/[entity]/
  list/route.ts      GET
  create/route.ts    POST
  update/route.ts    PUT
  delete/route.ts    DELETE — soft delete default
```

Always use `getDbWithAuth(request)` for Space/App data. Personal records use `personalDb()` / `getPersonalStore(request)` — `personal-storage.mdc`. Scope per app type.

## Response Envelope (mandatory)

```typescript
// Success
{ success: true, data: {...} }

// Error
{ success: false, code: "AUTH_401", error: "Human-readable message" }
```

| code | status | When |
|------|--------|------|
| `AUTH_401` | 401 | Missing/invalid token |
| `AUTH_403` | 403 | Not permitted |
| `VALIDATION_400` | 400 | Invalid fields |
| `NOT_FOUND_404` | 404 | Missing resource |
| `SERVER_500` | 500 | Server error |

## Shared app — list (GET)

```typescript
const filter: Record<string, unknown> = {
  group_id: user.group_id,
  status: { $ne: 'deleted' },
}
if (q) {
  filter.$or = [
    { name: { $regex: q, $options: 'i' } },
    { email: { $regex: q, $options: 'i' } },
  ]
}
```

## Personal store — list (GET)

```typescript
const { store, user } = getPersonalStore(request)
const items = await store.collection(COLLECTION).find(
  { status: { $ne: 'deleted' } },
  { sort: [['updated_at', -1]], limit: 50 }
)
```

No `group_id` / `user_id` in the filter. Dual-scope apps (`space,personal`): personal launch returns only this list; space launch merges personal + space (`personal-storage.mdc`).

## Dedicated app — list (GET)

```typescript
const filter: Record<string, unknown> = { status: { $ne: 'deleted' } }
// no group_id filter
```

## Personal store — create (POST)

```typescript
const { store, user } = getPersonalStore(request)
await store.collection(COLLECTION).insertOne({
  _id: nanoid(10),
  ...bodyFields,
  kind: 'personal',
  group_id: '0',
  created_by: user.user_id,
  created_at: now,
  updated_at: now,
  status: 'active',
})
```

Do not set `user_id`. Updates must be operators (`$set`). Soft-delete with `$set: { status: 'deleted' }`.

## Shared app — create (POST)

```typescript
const doc = {
  _id: nanoid(10),
  ...bodyFields,
  group_id: user.group_id,
  created_by: user.user_id,
  created_at: now,
